### Drill 8: Container Runtime (CRI) Diagnostics (`08-containerd-diagnostics/`)

When Kubernetes daemons (`kubelet` or API server) cannot provide telemetry, you must diagnose container lifecycle
directly via `crictl`.

#### Step 1: Configure `crictl` Endpoints

Verify that `crictl` communicates with containerd:

```bash
sudo crictl info
```

Ensure `/etc/crictl.yaml` points to `unix:///run/containerd/containerd.sock`.

#### Step 2: Inspect Containers and Pod Sandboxes

```bash
# List all active pods at the CRI level
sudo crictl pods

# List running containers
sudo crictl ps

# List all containers, including exited/crashed ones
sudo crictl ps -a

# View container logs directly from the runtime engine
sudo crictl logs <container-id>
```

#### Step 3: Run Runtime Verification Suite

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_cluster_troubleshooting_dir }}/08-containerd-diagnostics
./test-crictl.sh
